  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =A(x+1)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)+1 & =A(-1+1)+B \\\\ -1 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+1 & =A(0+1)-1 \\\\ 2 & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=2$ and $B=-1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
